<section class="atl-about">
  <h2 class="ref-sec-title">About the atlas</h2>
  <p>The atlas shows the <a href="/state/">states register</a>: every state, empire, principality and chiefdom the Institute has recorded, with the years it existed. A dot marks a state&#8217;s capital or seat, from Wikidata, not the extent of its territory; where no seat is known the state is placed in its present-day country and drawn as a ring. Years before the common era are approximate, and many early states are known only from a few sources.</p>
  <p>Read the world one age at a time in the <a href="/centuries/">century pages</a>, or a single land through time in the <a href="/countries/">country histories</a>.</p>
